WHAT THIS COVERS

The evidence corpus and the documents that govern it:

  src/data/evidence.json          the vetted entries and their citations
  src/data/taxonomy.ts            causes, self-check options, reader copy
  docs/EVIDENCE-VERIFICATION-LOG.md   how every citation was checked
  docs/PRINCIPLES.md              the voice and no-fabrication contract
  PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md           the product and design specs

The code is MIT licensed instead. See LICENSE.

WHY THESE TERMS

This is research writing, not software, and the work in it is the checking:
resolving every DOI, confirming registration, reading each abstract before a
claim was written, and recording the sources that were rejected and why.

  Attribution, because a corpus that has been verified this way should be
  traceable to how it was verified. If an entry is reused, a reader should be
  able to follow it back to the log that shows its working.

  ShareAlike, because a derived corpus that closes its sources would strip out
  the only thing that makes this one trustworthy.

Nothing here restricts quoting the underlying studies. Those belong to their
publishers, are cited in full, and are linked so anyone can read them directly.

